I want to start a service that generates Sockets for the CAN Modules.=20
Manually configuring the system is no problem, but I like to have it done=20
by yocto. Below I give the code of my recipe (socketcan.bb):
#########################
SUMMARY =3D "the config for the can socket interface"
SECTION =3D "CAN"
LICENSE =3D "CLOSED"

inherit update-rc.d

RDEPENDS=5F${PN} =3D "initscripts"

DEPENDS =3D "iproute2"

SRC=5FURI =3D "file://can=5Fif"

INITSCRIPT=5FPARAMS =3D "start 02 2 3 4 5 . stop 01 0 1 6 ."
INITSCRIPT=5FNAME =3D "can=5Fif"

CONFFILES=5F${PN} +=3D "${sysconfdir}/init.d/can=5Fif"
#########################
It has one file bash script "can=5Fif". This contains the up and down=20
commands. I want to generate at the /etc/rc*** Dirs the=20
S02can=5Fif/K01can=5Fif links.
Building the recipe via "bitbake socketcan" works fine.
When generating the rootfs via "bitbake core-image-minimal" I got the=20
following error:
